---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: collections.subjectPages
  size: 1
  alias: subject
permalink: "/s/{{ subject.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ subject.title | safe }}"
---
<article class="subject">
  <header class="subject-head{% if subject.essays | length %} no-rule{% endif %}">
    {#- The subject's sky at the one size where the full three-curtain scene
        is properly legible. Small renders elsewhere use the chip variant.
        From 58rem the page takes the daily's shell (2026-11-03) and this is
        its lone card in the art column, the way an essay's is: the header's
        text, the essays and the fragments all start at the daily's text
        column, so the two kinds of page read at one width (style.css, the
        margin column). Below 58rem it stays the cover beside the title. -#}
    {%- if subject.coverUrl %}
    <span class="sky sky-cover{% if subject.coverBox %} sky-box{% endif %}{% if subject.coverPixel %} sky-pixel{% endif %}" style="background-image:url({{ subject.coverUrl }}){% if subject.coverBox %};--box:{{ subject.coverBox }}{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    {%- else %}
    <span class="sky" style="background-image:url({{ subject.skyUrl }})" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    {%- endif %}
    <div>
      {#- The way from a subject back to its group (2026-11-03): for a
          demoted group's subject the only path to its canon and shelf, which
          hang off the group's page. -#}
      {%- set g = groupInfo[subject.group] %}
      {% if g %}<a class="group-link" href="{{ g.urls.home }}">{{ g.label }} ›</a>{% endif %}
      <h1>{{ subject.title }}</h1>
      {#- One square per day written about, long gaps folded into a labelled
          break, running on to today on active subjects. See foldStrip. -#}
      {% if subject.litDays %}
      <p class="lit-days{% if subject.litDays.clipped %} clipped{% endif %}" style="--le:{{ subject.litDays.pal.edge }};--lm:{{ subject.litDays.pal.mid }};--ld:{{ subject.litDays.pal.deep }};--lg:{{ subject.litDays.pal.glow }}" aria-label="Days written about, {{ subject.litDays.first }} to {{ subject.litDays.last }}">
        {%- for seg in subject.litDays.segments %}{% if seg.gap %}<span class="gap{% if seg.tail %} tail{% endif %}">{{ seg.gap }}</span>{% else %}{% for d in seg.days %}<span class="{% if d.lit %}on{% endif %}{% if d.today %} today{% endif %}"{% if d.lit %} style="--i:{{ d.i }};--h:{{ d.h }}px"{% endif %} title="{{ d.key }}{% if d.lit %} · {{ d.words }} words{% endif %}"></span>{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
      </p>
      {% endif %}
      {#- The chips follow the group's bands: status where it has a shelf,
          the verdict where it has a canon. A bandless subject (Aurora
          Watch, a league) has neither, and the row goes unless it has tags. -#}
      {%- set isMedium = g and (g.hasShelf or g.hasCanon) %}
      {% if isMedium or subject.tags | length %}
      <p class="subject-meta">
        {#- Canon is the top rung, but it leads the row and goes gold, and it
            links to /canon/ — the ten, their history, the essays about them
            — rather than to the bare /r/canon/ view. -#}
        {% if subject.canon %}<a class="badge badge-g b-canon" href="{{ g.urls.canon if g else '/canon/' }}">canon</a>{% endif %}
        {% if g and g.hasShelf %}
        <span class="badge b-{{ subject.status }}">{{ subject.status | statusWord(subject.group) }}</span>
        {% endif %}
        {% if g and g.hasCanon %}
        {#- The rating, as a chip linking to its rung's view — every game
            rated the same word, which is how the word calibrates itself. A
            canon subject's rung is the gold badge above, not a second chip.
            Unrated renders "pending" here too, unlinked, so a subject page
            never looks like the field was forgotten. -#}
        {% if subject.canon %}{% elif subject.rating %}<a class="rating r-{{ subject.rating.slug }}" href="/r/{{ subject.rating.slug }}/">{{ subject.rating.title }}</a>{% else %}<a class="rating r-pending" href="/r/">pending</a>{% endif %}
        {% endif %}
        {#- Sidestepping to the franchise or the genre is the natural next move
            for a reader who arrived by following a title, so the tags sit in the
            meta row rather than at the foot of a long timeline. -#}
        {% if subject.tags | length %}
        <span class="tag-list">
          {% for tag in subject.tags %}<a class="tag-link" href="/t/{{ tag.slug }}/">#{{ tag.slug }}</a>{% endfor %}
        </span>
        {% endif %}
      </p>
      {% endif %}
      {#- The standing blurb: undated, revisable, the subject's one paragraph
          for when a whole article would be absurd but the page shouldn't read
          as blank. Lives beside the cover, above the header rule. -#}
      {% if subject.blurbHtml %}
      <div class="subject-blurb">{{ subject.blurbHtml | safe }}</div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </header>

  {#- A cards group's cards head the page of the subject they belong to
      (2026-11-03: the Bears and their vibe line on NFL, the Cubs on MLB):
      the card, then why Hat follows them. Anchored, so the group page's
      band can link straight to one. -#}
  {%- from "cards.njk" import row %}
  {%- set myCards = subject | cardsFor(collections.groupPages) %}
  {% if myCards | length %}
  <section class="team-cards">
    {% for c in myCards %}{{ row(c) }}{% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {#- Essays pinned first: the most considered writing on the page shouldn't
      sit buried under a replay's fragments. Lede + link only — full text has
      exactly one home, the essay's own /e/ page. Subject pages pin; tag views
      keep essays inline in the stream instead. -#}
  {% if subject.essays | length %}
  <section class="essays">
    <h2 class="section-head">Deep thoughts</h2>
    {% for essay in subject.essays %}
    <div class="fragment">
      <a class="essay-title" href="{{ essay.url }}">{{ essay.title }}</a>
      <a class="fragment-date" href="{{ essay.url }}">{{ essay.date | readableDate }}</a>
      <p class="tag-essay">{{ essay.blurb }}</p>
      <a class="more" href="{{ essay.url }}">read →</a>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if subject.fragments | length %}
  <section class="timeline">
    {% if subject.essays | length %}<h2 class="section-head">Along the way</h2>{% endif %}
    {% for fragment in subject.fragments %}
    <div class="fragment">
      {#- Back to the section in its day. A section that wore a face (`##
          Bears` on NFL's page) says so beside its date. -#}
      <a class="fragment-date" href="{{ fragment.anchorUrl }}">{{ fragment.date | readableDate }}</a>{% if fragment.face %} <span class="fragment-face">{{ fragment.face.title }}</span>{% endif %}
      {{ fragment.html | safe }}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% elif not (subject.essays | length or subject.blurbHtml) %}
  <p class="empty">Nothing written about this yet.</p>
  {% endif %}
</article>
